{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Yitnaseḥ</b> — destroyed, like יִסַּח ה' יֶהֶרֵס (he uproots — YHWH destroys), and similarly <i>mishmeret ha-bayit</i>: מְסַח — he commanded that they guard <i>mishmeret ha-bayit</i>, the place of destruction, so no person enters from there." "<b>U-zaqif</b> — an allusion to walls and to pillars that stand, and its counterpart: זוֹקֵף — raises bent ones, and its meaning is 'lifts,' or 'causes to stand.' Likewise the Targum of וַיִּשָּׂא עֵינָיו, and its meaning is: the one standing shall be destroyed upon the timber." "<b>Nulu</b> — fastened, like וְשָׂמוּהוּ לְמוֹצָאוֹת. And in the language of our Rabbis of blessed memory: <i>menolta</i>."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:07.622462271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}